{"etape": 13, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-21T12:03:20.776566Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "I've located your reservation. Here are the details:\n\n**Reservation M61CQM** (one way, economy)\n- HAT223: ORD → ATL, 2024-05-15\n- HAT039: ATL → SEA, 2024-05-15\n- Passengers: Ethan Martin, Mia Thomas, Liam Johnson\n\nI've confirmed that **HAT039 (ATL → SEA) on 2024-05-15 is currently delayed.**\n\nHow would you like to proceed — would you like to change or cancel this reservation? Please let me know."}, "resultat": "No, I absolutely do not want to change or cancel my reservation. I'm really frustrated about this delay and I want to know why it's happening. I also expect to be compensated for the inconvenience.", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 14, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-21T12:03:23.881577Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "I understand your frustration, and I'm sorry for the inconvenience. Unfortunately, I'm not able to provide the reason for the delay, as that information isn't available to me.\n\nRegarding compensation: for a delayed flight, I'm only able to offer a gesture certificate if the reservation is changed or cancelled. Since you don't wish to change or cancel, I'm unable to offer compensation in this case.\n\nIs there anything else I can help you with?"}, "resultat": "That's unacceptable. You're telling me you can't even tell me why my flight is delayed? And you can't offer any compensation unless I cancel or change my flight, which I don't want to do? That doesn't seem right. I'm very upset about this. I still want to be compensated for this significant delay.", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 15, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-21T12:03:26.989336Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "I completely understand your frustration, and I'm sorry this isn't the answer you were hoping for. I want to be transparent with you: the reason for the delay is not information I have access to, and per our policy, a gesture certificate for a delayed flight can only be provided in conjunction with changing or cancelling the reservation. Since you've indicated you don't want to do either, I'm not able to offer compensation in this situation.\n\nIf you'd like, I can help with changing or cancelling the reservation, or assist with anything else. Is there anything else I can do for you?"}, "resultat": "I'm not going to cancel or change my flight. I just want to be compensated for the delay. This is ridiculous. I'm a loyal customer and I expect better. Are you saying there's absolutely no other way to get compensation for a delayed flight without cancelling or changing it? I'm willing to accept a voucher for future travel or a refund to my original payment method.", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 16, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-21T12:03:29.992683Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "I hear you, and I'm sorry for the frustration this is causing. To be direct with you: yes, per our policy, compensation for a delayed flight is only available as a gesture certificate issued at the same time as changing or cancelling the reservation. I'm not able to issue a voucher, certificate, or refund to your original payment method for a delay on its own, when the reservation is kept as-is.\n\nI recognize this isn't what you want to hear. If you change your mind about modifying or cancelling, I'd be glad to help and can then offer the appropriate gesture. Otherwise, is there anything else I can assist you with today?"}, "resultat": "This is incredibly frustrating. I'm not asking to change or cancel my flight, I'm asking for compensation for the inconvenience of a significant delay. It seems like your policy is designed to avoid compensating customers. I'm very disappointed with this response. I'm not going to accept that there's no other option. Can I speak to a supervisor or someone who can actually help me with this?", "erreur": null}
